# B0 (PRE-WINDOW, no card opened, production keeps serving): build the SHIPPING base image tp4-serve-9 from this branch: the four-seat best-levers traffic
# candidate c2-packed-tp4-best-ship baked in as the image's serving default and THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as that profile's max-num-seqs (4, computed by
# the build script from the context's own profiles file). C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE is the one key that does it: a build without it (every other tag, production's
# included) bakes nothing and its default stays qwen_c2_profiles.json's c2-packed-tp4. The profile is a traffic profile (not gate_only, P150x4), which the job
# parser requires of anything baked.
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists on the host, so a reused tag would silently serve an old image.
# READ: the build log's provenance report: '(c) the image default is the BAKED profile c2-packed-tp4-best-ship', no problem line, and 'baking the serving default
# c2-packed-tp4-best-ship with a session cap of 4'; the closure checks pass; the build prints the image id. Never run it during a timing job (a busy host skews timed phases).
# Duration (estimate): 20-60 min (most layers cached). Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window before production is touched.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-4 four-seat SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9 is the SHIPPING base B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-4 commit with the candidate profile
# c2-packed-tp4-best-ship baked in as the image's serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its seat count (4). Every job
# serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default.
# qwen_c2_profiles.json's own default stays c2-packed-tp4: only a build that names C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE (B0's one key) bakes anything. A commit that
# changes a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
